$ dorc why 10 --book=book.sh -o firewall.oracle.sh -o package.oracle.sh --risk-faultless-skips --results=probe-results.txt
      [ book.sh, participating lines:
    9 | apt-get install -y oldpkg
   10 | ufw allow 443/tcp

   [unwritten: why-participating-lines-closure]

   === OUTCOME ===

   10|ufw skipped RATHER THAN guarded: 9|apt-get ran above it, which normally forces an
   apply-time guard-clause; but --risk-faultless-skips activates acting on authors' at-most
   claims, and that claim does not reach what the skip was reported on.

   === ANALYSIS ===

   10|ufw being skipped stood on all of the following, together:

   * firewall.oracle.sh:5   reported  "sm.dorc.Firewall:443/tcp@allowed" (received 02:00:37,
                                      rc 0)
   * firewall.oracle.sh:17  vouches   "re-running this line adds nothing worth running
                                      while sm.dorc.Firewall:443/tcp holds"
   ! package.oracle.sh:24   claims    "`apt-get` touches AT MOST {sm.dorc.Package:oldpkg}"

      This speaks for everything it did NOT measure. Fact derived from as-written contract
      only; no run can back it.

         [ package.oracle.sh, as-written:
      24 |       install|purge) printf '%s\n' "$1" : disturbs sm.dorc.Package ;;

   * dorc                   derives   that claim is proven disjoint from
                                      sm.dorc.Firewall:443/tcp -- it does not overlap what
                                      was reported

   `!` marks the link that covers unmeasurable things; the class of information no runnable
   command could test.

   so: nothing 9|apt-get claims to touch overlaps sm.dorc.Firewall:443/tcp, which is what
   the skip was reported on; the skip stood.

   === NEXT STEPS ===

   if 10|ufw SHOULD have run:

      suspect:  the 9|apt-get claim -- the only link speaking for unmeasured state. if it
                also touches sm.dorc.Firewall:443/tcp, it is what wrongly kept this line
                out.

      fix:      package.oracle.sh:24 (widen the claim; every consumer heals)
   OR
      fix:      `dorc plan <book> <host>` (run without --risk-faultless-skips, to distrust
                oracle-authored claims)

      verify:   `dorc plan <book> <host>` (re-measures the world as it is now; a fact that
                came back wrong comes back diverged, and the line returns)
      review:   `dorc why book.sh:10 --all` (every link, unselected, exhaustive)

